From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 1047 redfin: camera cutout ring (kern.sweet_cutout_aa)

An anti-aliased black disc over the selfie-camera hole (LineageOS redfin
cutout: centre 81,77, radius 39-40 panel px) hides the panel's jagged
edge around it. kern.sweet_cutout_aa 0 off (default), 1 CPU disc drawn
into each direct frame after its fence, 2 display engine: DMA0 staged on
LM0 over the VIGs with a premultiplied 128x128 ARGB layer in splash
memory (0xa2100000), set up once, no per-frame cost, also in the blit
path. Geometry kern.sweet_cutout_x16/_y16/_r16/_aa16 or
p cutout MODE [X16 Y16 R16 AA16]; SWEET CUTOUT 5 s line while on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC2ugyLE29nbFLJoQZd
---
